{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032716-m20-character-help-technocratic-survivor","id":1032716,"title":"M20 Character Help-Technocratic Survivor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-16T09:30:33-08:00","id":1032716,"title":"M20 Character Help-Technocratic Survivor","content":"I need help trying to make a character for a M20 game, a technocatic survivor post-fall of the TU as a whole with the discovery of the higher ups being corrupted. Story wise he awakened when the Lab was reclaimed by Pentex and exposure to some wyrm monster and paradox incursion resulted in the place being shunted elsewhere. The survivor was a animal handler/extraordinary citizen, the Lab he was employed at dealt with brain boosting drugs to combat diseases and conditions that target the brain. First resulting side project was a SMART Dog program, some animals the drugs were tested on developed positive boost of intelligence. He was hired to train the animals and administer regular specialized diets. He was able to escape with one SMART Dog downside is because the Lab went under the resources for the special diet has become harder to get. The SMART Dog he was able to save is a augmented wolf dog that was at some point under control of DNA.<br /> <br /> He is a Orphan tradition wise, sphere of magic not sure quite yet but still he clings to the old paradigm of technocracy because its the only thing he was exposed to prior to awakening. He uses very little 'magic', mostly brews up al/chemicaI cocktails to boost him or his companion so they can get what they need. I appreciate help, how can I make this character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:19:02-08:00","id":1032872,"title":"","content":"Seems like he's just &quot;technically&quot; an Orphan in that he doesn't have a Sect to fall back on. More a &quot;social&quot; Orphan than an actual &quot;my magic is my own thing&quot; Orphan. (Though, without someone to talk about... or people who's ideas will cause him to start taking off in directions different, he might end up as an Orphan.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, he seems like he's a Progenitor or Progenitor derived. It depends on what he wants those chemical cocktails to accomplish, but Life seems like a lock for one of his Spheres. Mind as well (psychoactive pharmaceuticals anyone?) From some of the other aspects of his backstory, he might be parting from the accepted Union paradigm by a little bit of Spirit. Probably, I dunno, Life 3 for sure.... Mind up to 3 and keep it cool on Spirit with 1 (for now). Obviously Arete 3. I really see him having an injection gun, inserting a cartridge filled with some fluid he made up in a makeshift lab, putting it to his carotid and shooting up. Otherwise things might start going a very &quot;junkie&quot; direction. Just concocting potions doesn't seem as fitting with a baseline Technocratic Union paradigm/training. Though, I guess, some things might work taken orally (though oral liquid medicine just doesn't have the same psychological oomph as injection...)<br /> <br /> If he's mixing things up, he might warrant a little Matter, but it doesn't seem in line with what you're saying that he might make... an acid wash that turns, say, Pyrex into pure sodium. (Very effective when used on most gym water bottles if you are looking for a big explosion...)<br /> <br /> I would recommend against having the doggie be a Familiar, as there seems to be little reason for it to be eating Paradox with the backstory as is, in which case it's a Retainer or Ally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T14:37:14-08:00","id":1033655,"title":"","content":"I was talking to the ST and we figured out the SMART Dog I rescued was actually werewolf kinfolk to a local Glasswalker branch so they approached my character in human guise before game and take their relative back. Apologies for the inconvenience and hand a burn phone with contacts to their corporate HQ incase he ran afoul of the things that took over the labs. As the place went up in paradox he saw some of the other projects going on inside and it shook him up, he has a distrust for the Progenitors and might be being hunted by them. One of the reasons he was hired besides his ability was his innate connection dealing with animals. ST alluded it might be I was kinfolk not in the know but it was up to me. The Glasswalkers are Allies I can only call in if its something Wyrm related.<br /> <br /> I'm definitely thinking Life and Mind as his primary spheres. Life would let him to control and manipulate lifeforms if needed plus healing. Mind will let him force the pack mentality and impose his will on others. They're more subtle to him and not overtly magical if he sticks with the paradigm he was imprinted with that isn't perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T18:12:21-08:00","id":1033777,"title":"","content":"Not sure if I helped or not, but it sounds like you have nailed down most of what you needed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:53:33-08:00","id":1033842,"title":"","content":"Prime would also fit rather well. Enhancing living things by imbuing with your resonance. You can also take Matter and use/create nanobots or synthetic implants to replace organs and things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:04:19-08:00","id":1034121,"title":"","content":"Still and all... with the Kinfolk angle, the &quot;what horrors he saw&quot; in Wyrm-tainted facility, and other dangling Garou-related sub-plot threads, Spirit 1 seems like it is HIGHLY in order.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't go for Matter as it's not going to help out with cybernetics, etc. until fairly high levels. It's basically alchemy at 2-3. And were cybernetics an issue? He seemed like he dealt exclusively with biotech, particularly magic-laced biotech. Unless there is a &quot;materials science/chemistry&quot; angle that doesn't have to do with biochem, Matter is probably not the way way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:31:20-08:00","id":1036739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032716-m20-character-help-technocratic-survivor?p=1034121#post1034121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still and all... with the Kinfolk angle, the &quot;what horrors he saw&quot; in Wyrm-tainted facility, and other dangling Garou-related sub-plot threads, Spirit 1 seems like it is HIGHLY in order.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't go for Matter as it's not going to help out with cybernetics, etc. until fairly high levels. It's basically alchemy at 2-3. And were cybernetics an issue? He seemed like he dealt exclusively with biotech, particularly magic-laced biotech. Unless there is a &quot;materials science/chemistry&quot; angle that doesn't have to do with biochem, Matter is probably not the way way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He primarily dealt with animals and was given the special food stuff for his animals he handled. I might pick up matter on the lower end for the biochem/tech later once the chronicle sets up the proper contacts. ST said I'll be considered kinfolk of the Glasswalkers on edge about a job offer they are handing me. Because of my survivor being a life/mind/spirit 'mage' he is perfect for tending to lupus and others things that fall under their supervision in the project to set up a wolf haven under their banner..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}